  "question": {
    "text": "Benzene and toluene form nearly ideal solutions. At $20^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$, the vapour pressure of benzene is 75 torr and that of toluene is 22 torr. The partial vapour pressure of benzene at $20^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ for a solution containing $78 \\mathrm{~g}$ of benzene and $46 \\mathrm{~g}$ of toluene in torr is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
